# The README frame: connect to SQL Server, open bench → Tables in the tree,
# type a statement in the pad and run it. `scripts/readme-frame.sh` replays
# this at 100x28 and writes the frame it names into README.md, so the picture
# in the README is output and never a drawing. The container
# `scripts/db-up.sh` starts has to be up, and the pad needs a state directory
# of its own or it starts with whatever the last run typed.

key c
wait busy
expect ● local-mssql

# dbo is the schema a login lands in and is open already, so bench — the one
# the seed wrote into — is six rows below it: counted from the top rather
# than from the bottom, since a schema somebody else leaves behind sorts
# after it and G would land on that instead.
key g
key j
key j
key j
key j
key j
key j
key l
expect ▾ bench
key j
key l
wait busy
expect customers

key Tab
type select id, name, country, credit_limit
key Enter
type from bench.customers where country in ('DE', 'NO', 'IE')

# A frame is dumped one terminal cell per character, so a glyph drawn two
# cells wide comes out as itself and a space and the columns after it lean.
# The countries here are the ones whose names are narrow, which keeps the
# picture in the README straight; scripts/qa/query-workflow.sh is where the
# wide ones are checked.

# Long enough for the pad to be written, so the title is not [modified].
wait 600
key Ctrl-R
wait busy
expect ╭ Results ·
expect Zoë Bauer

frame readme
key Ctrl-Q
